Netscape Navigator Personal Edition V1.2 for Windows 3.1 and Windows 95

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Everything in a single software package

o  Automatic registration with choice of Internet service provider

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

Digital has expanded its reselling agreement with Netscape Communications,
Inc., to include Netscape Navigator Personal Edition V1.2 for Windows 3.1
and Windows 95 software, which gives PC users one-button access to the
Internet.

Netscape Navigator Personal Edition delivers access to the Internet to
anyone with a PC and modem. It includes

o  All the features of the original Netscape Navigator

o  Eudora Light e-mail from QUALCOMM (lets users send and receive e-mail,
   create personal address books and distribution lists, attach files
   including graphics and sound, and read and create e-mail offline to
   reduce access charges)

o  Network TeleSystems protocol software for TCP/IP connectivity to the
   Internet

o  ShivaPPP client software from Shiva Corporation, which provides users
   with high performance, reliable remote-access connectivity at bandwidths
   of 14.4 or higher -- offers multiple simultaneous loading of text and
   images.

o  Netscape Navigator Personal Edition incorporates the Secure Sockets Layer
   (SSL) protocol and RSA encryption technologies for integrated security --
   when used in conjunction with a secure server, a user can communicate
   financial or other confidential information safely.

As part of its new product offering, Netscape has teamed with Internet
Service Providers (ISPs), including MCI Communications Corporation, NETCOM
OnLine Communications Services, Portal Information Network, and UUNET
Technologies, Inc., to ensure that Personal Edition users can choose the
most reliable and cost effective Internet access more easily than ever
before.

When first installed, the Registration Wizard presents a short series of
one-button online forms that guide users through the installation process
and connects them to Netscape's hypermedia list of available ISPs. Once the
user selects one, the software automatically sets up an account with the
chosen provider. From then on, Netscape Navigator Personal Edition dials the
service provider directly when launched.

BENEFITS

o  Quick setup and configuration -- Without complicated communications
   protocols or modem scripts

o  Everything in one package -- Includes everything needed to access all the
   important Internet resources including the World Wide Web, e-mail, news
   groups, Gopher and FTP sites

o  An easy and intuitive interface -- Offers simple point-and-click access
   to information on Internet Bookmarks, directory buttons, and a
   customizable toolbar to make Internet navigation easy

o  Advanced features -- Offers the latest browse features including full
   HTML 3.0 support, fully threaded news reading, and MIME-compliant news
   reading and posting to allow for generation of multimedia news articles

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

Netscape Navigator Personal Edition V1.2 is available now for sale in the
U.S. and Canada. An international version of the product will be released
later.

Digital is offering Generic Right-to-Copy licenses in increments of 10 to
10,000. These packages are version/platform generic. To be eligible, the
user must purchase one complete kit of the Personal Edition for each
platform.  For example:  A 100 Right-to-Copy license pack may be used for 50
copies on UNIX, 25 on MAC, 10 on Windows, and 15 on Windows 95.

A complete range of software support, update, and license subscription
services are available on a worldwide basis. Users have the option to
purchase Telephone Support Services, a New Version License Subscription
Service, a Packaged Service that provides right to use new versions and
updates to the software, and the Documentation Update Distribution Service.

