DECnet/OSI V6.3 for OpenVMS

DECnet/OSI V6.3 for OpenVMS systems updates and enhances the capabilities of
Digital's network transports product set. DECnet/OSI V6.3 for OpenVMS now
offers a new cluster configuration capability that allows all members of a
cluster to be configured from a single workstation. This feature allows for
faster upgrades of clusters.

DECnet/OSI V6.3 for OpenVMS now includes the OSI Application Programming
Interfaces previously available in the OSI Application Developer's Toolkit.
A new interface to the OSI Session Layer is also being introduced in this
version.

DECnet/OSI V6.3 for OpenVMS will be available via the Internet and magnetic
tape media in October 1995. It will ship on the OpenVMS Alpha CD-ROM in
November 1995 and on the OpenVMS VAX CD-ROM in December 1995.

For complete ordering information, see the "DECnet/OSI V6.2 for OpenVMS VAX
and Alpha" article in the June issue of Customer Update.




