AlphaServer 1000 4/266 System

HIGHLIGHTS

o  High performance, reliable server for PC LAN, Internet access, database,
   or other business critical applications

o  Affordable, high availability solutions through clustering to workgroups
   and small- to medium-sized businesses

o  Member of the Internet AlphaServer family for Digital UNIX and Windows
   NT; provides everything needed to create and maintain a home page on the
   World Wide Web

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The AlphaServer 1000 4/266 system is a 266 MHz Alpha server in a deskside
tower enclosure that supports up to 1 GB of RAM, and runs Digital UNIX,
OpenVMS, or Windows NT software. It replaces the AlphaServer 1000 4/233 at
the same price. The system was designed to offer investment protection
through easy CPU daughtercard upgrades to faster processors. Expandability
using PC industry-standard components, such as 72-pin 36 bit SIMMs, provides
outstanding system performance at an affordable price. The following
components are integrated on the system motherboard:

o  Industry standard SVGA controller
o  Floppy disk controller
o  Two serial ports and one parallel port
o  Keyboard and mouse controller
o  LCD operator control panel
o  PCI-based fast SCSI-2 controller

The AlphaServer 1000 is well suited for use as a PC LAN server for a large
number of users, or a database or applications server. It is available as a
packaged Internet server for Digital UNIX, or, with a separately available
Internet Software Kit, a user can build one to individual specifications.

Windows NT Web AlphaServer systems, based on the AlphaServer 1000 4/266, are
a subset of the Internet AlphaServer family, and provide everything needed
to create and maintain an operational home page on the World Wide Web. (For
more information on this product, see the "NT Web AlphaServer Systems"
