HIGHLIGHTS

o  Cost-effective, entry level server for small- to medium-sized workgroups
   and businesses

o  Most affordable cluster-ready system available

o  Ideal PC LAN server, or replicated site or application server; ideal for
   migration from the MicroVAX 3100

o  Member of the Internet AlphaServer family for Digital UNIX and Windows
   NT; provides everything needed to maintain a home page on the World Wide
   Web

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The AlphaServer 400 4/233 is a cost-effective entry-level uniprocessor
system that supports up to 384 MB of industry-standard SIMM memory, and
offers a choice of Digital UNIX, Windows NT, or OpenVMS operating systems.

The AlphaServer 400 4/233 includes

o  A 233 MHz processor
o  An integral Fast Narrow SCSI-2 controller
o  Industry-standard I/O, with 2 PCI, 3 ISA, and 1 PCI/ISA slots
o  Five drive bays for a total of 17.2 GB of internal disk storage, using
   the 4.3 GB disk drive
o  Screwless deskside minitower enclosure that makes configuring and
   servicing quick and easy
o  Remote diagnostics port accessible through a simple serial link
o  Three-year onsite hardware warranty

PCI-based RAID, FDDI, and asynchronous multiplexers are just some of the
higher performance options available on the new system. Support for the ISA
WAN Synchronous Communications controller makes the AlphaServer 400 a solid
choice for the X.25, DECnet/OSI, and SNA WAN communications environments and
businesses with remote branches that are looking to support a small number
of users inexpensively.

This AlphaServer 400 is flexible and powerful enough to serve as a PC LAN
server (for files, printing, and e-mail), a database and application server,
or a communications gateway. It is available as a packaged Internet server
for Digital UNIX, or it can be custom built by ordering the Internet
Software Kit. NT Web AlphaServer systems based on the AlphaServer 400 4/233
are a subset of the Internet AlphaServer family, and provide everything
needed to create and maintain an operational home page on the World Wide
Web. (For more information on this product, see the "NT Web AlphaServer
systems" article in this issue of Customer Update.)

Remote diagnosis allows resellers and system administrators to call in,
remotely run diagnostics, configure the system, and/or recommend a fix or
pull a part. Support costs are mnimized because onsite visits and service
calls are reduced. With Digital's clustering software on Digital UNIX,
OpenVMS, and soon, Windows NT, the AlphaServer 400 4/233 offers the
industry's most affordable, high availability solution for under $25,000.

