PrintServer 32 plus Printer

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Powerhouse and rugged laser printing for large workgroups and data
   centers

o  Seamless integration into Digital, PC, and UNIX operating environments

o  Price/performance surpasses competition

o  PRInt Status Manager (PRISM) software for managing local and remote
   printers without leaving the desk

o  Upgrade Kits available for PrintServer 32 and turbo PrintServer 20
   printers

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The PrintServer 32 plus printer and PrintServer Software V5.1 products work
together to offer users rugged laser printing capabilities for large
workgroups and data centers.

PrintServer 32 plus

The PrintServer 32 plus is Digital's new high volume, ruggedly reliable
laser printer that replaces the PrintServer 32 printer. The PrintServer 32
plus has a rated engine speed of 32 impressions per minute and a rugged duty
cycle of 200,000 pages per month. It offers all the capabilities of the
PrintServer 32, with more resident page description languages and fonts, a
higher duty cycle, and more print management tools.

The PrintServer 32 plus provides shared printing for users of popular
Digital, PC, and UNIX systems on DECnet and TCP/IP Ethernet networks,
including Windows NT, Windows 95, SunOS, HP-UX, IBM-AIX, SCO UNIX, Silicon
Graphics IRIX, Digital UNIX, Novell NetWare, Solaris, ULTRIX, and OpenVMS
systems. It bundles PostScript Level 2 and HP-PCL5 printer languages, always
switching quietly and reliably between both printer languages as users
submit print jobs from a mixture of applications. Digital also supports
applications that are not PostScript or PCL through its host based
translators.

PrintServer Software V5.1

PrintServer Software V5.1 provides Digital's industry leading network
printer management software, which allows MIS managers to monitor and manage
their local and remote printers without leaving their desks. Printing and
printer management software makes network printing faster and easier by
providing solutions that address the needs of people at all levels.

PRInt Status Manager (PRISM) is an easy to use graphical user interface that
alerts MIS managers to the printing status of their printers or groups of
printers in a color-coded fashion. This allows MIS managers to immediately
recognize and diagnose the status of all their network printers. For
example, if a printer is idle or printing, a PRISM icon will report back a
"ready," "idle," or similar message and be color coded green; if supplies
are low, a PRISM icon will report back a "supplies" message and be color
coded yellow. PRISM also allows printers to be grouped together; for
example, by building, department, or floor.

PrintServer 32/20 Upgrade Kit

The PrintServer 32/20 Upgrade Kit is available for PrintServer 32 and turbo
PrintServer 20 owners. With the installation of the Upgrade Kit, users can
take full advantage of all the new features and capabilities of the
PrintServer Software V5.1. The Upgrade Kit includes a boot ROM, firmware,
memory, a PostScript Level 2 license, and an installation guide. To maximize
performance and ensure that all features/functionality are enabled, it is
recommended that turbo PrintServer 20 and PrintServer 32 users install the
Upgrade Kit when running PrintServer Software V5.1.

BENEFITS

PrintServer 32 plus

o  Improved printing speeds -- With print speeds of up to 32 impressions per
   minute, users will see tremendous speed improvements over their personal
   and shared laser printers

o  Uninterrupted run times -- Large input and output trays allow for longer,
   uninterrupted run times and less frequent loading of trays

o  Network connections -- The direct Ethernet connection ensures easy access
   to all users in wide area and local area networks, thereby eliminating
   transmission speed bottlenecks

o  Sorting capability -- MailBox provides a sorting capability that assists
   in keeping the print area tidy, keeping print jobs organized so that less
   jobs are lost, and minimizing reprinting

o  Paper support -- A variety of paper sizes are supported, including large
   format, which helps companies meet their overall printing needs

PrintServer Software V5.1

o  Print management capabilities -- Delivers extensive printer management
   capabilities and support for SNMP that allows easy printer management,
   monitoring, and administration of local and remote printers all from a
   central desktop.

o  Multiple platform support -- Multiple network operating systems,
   platforms, and languages work together seamlessly so that all users on
   the network can access all the printing resources.

o  Centralized accounting -- Job accounting allows users to be charged on a
   per-job basis and identifies print usage on a per printer basis.

o  Image enhancement -- DECimage resolution enhancement makes images appear
   as if they were printed on a 1,000 dpi printer.

o  Flexibility and compatibility -- Support for PostScript Level 2 and PCL 5
   printer languages provides flexibility and compatibility with
   applications in mixed platform environments switching automatically and
   reliably between printer languages.

o  Reliability -- Auto-error recovery ensures that no pages are lost or
   duplicated, and that no reprinting is required.

o  Integration -- Native lpd support provides ease of use and integration
   into UNIX printing environments.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The PrintServer 32 plus printer, PrintServer Software V5.1, and PrintServer
32/20 upgrade kit are available now.

