PATHWORKS V6.0 for DOS and Windows

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Simplifies PC access to networked resources and sharing of information

o  Improves administration of resources and information across multiple
   network operating systems (NOS) environments

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

PATHWORKS V6.0 for DOS and Windows client software is PC integration
software that integrates complex, multivendor environments. The software
also provides value-added features over and above the PC industry's major
network operating systems, including DOS, Windows, Windows for Workgroups,
Windows 95, LAN Manager, and NetWare clients.

Due to the overwhelming amount and diversity of information that users have
a need to find and use, as well as the explosive growth of the Internet,
PATHWORKS V6 for DOS and Windows has extended its solutions to focus on
providing information integration capabilities. PATHWORKS V6.0 for DOS and
Windows removes the barriers from finding and accessing information, both
resources (file and print shares), as well as data. PATHWORKS V6.0 for DOS
and Windows makes it easier for users to access and share information, and
gives administrators an easy way to manage resources and information across
multiple network operating systems (NOS) environments.

BENEFITS

PATHWORKS V6.0 for DOS and Windows offers a number of new benefits for users
on the Windows and Windows for Workgroups platforms. (Refer to the
"PATHWORKS Support for Windows 95" article in the August 8, 1995 Customer
Update for information regarding PATHWORKS functionality for Windows 95).
These are:

o  Advanced network connection services that allow users to search for
   shared printers and files based upon meaningful attributes, such as
   searches for "color PostScript printers on the second floor, north wing."
   This capability is implemented in the Network Connect application and is
   made possible by the new Directory Assistant technology in PATHWORKS
   software.

o  New management utilities associated with Directory Assistant capabilities
   allow administrators to quickly and easily gather network information on
   shared printers and files. These management utilities allow
   administrators to easily set up their directory environment and
   synchronize naming across diverse elements of their environment.

o  Password assistant capabilities mean that users need only remember a
   single password to gain access to their network resources.

o  Automatic print driver loading capabilities reduce the time required for
   a user to use a new printer.

o  New, protected mode versions of the DECnet, LAT, CTERM, and Telnet
   transports free up precious conventional memory for use by other
   applications on Windows for Workgroups desktops.

o  The previous, separately packaged PATHWORKS remote software is now fully
   integrated, thereby simplifying its installation and allowing easy
   switching between LAN and WAN connections. Other remote and mobile access
   enhancements include the ability to establish connections through a
   Windows dialer application for all WAN types (asynchronous, ISDN, X.25,
   and X.32); increased security while using PPP with PAP/CHAP
   authentication; and CAPI 2 support, which allows a wide choice of ISDN
   cards from many vendors (including PCMCIA ISDN cards).

o  The Workgroup Web application provides shared web capabilities that allow
   users in diverse locations to organize and share information through the
   enhanced Windows based Mosaic browser. The Mosaic browser includes
   built-in JPEG and GIF viewer facilities, an easy-to-use toolbar, and the
   ability to display multiple windows.

o  Improved license management capabilities, including performance
   improvements that minimize the time required to obtain a license from the
   license server, reducing the amount of memory needed for the client
   licensing software, and better integration of Windows for Workgroups
   clients.

o  PATHWORKS V6.0 for DOS and Windows supports NetWare client VLM networking
   software, which allows users more choice of network operating systems
   types.

o  Enhanced configuration capabilities allow users to remotely configure
   Windows for Workgroups clients.

o  Quick and easy access to the PATHWORKS Information Shelf (online
   documentation) through the addition of a clickable table of contents and
   a full-text search engine allows users to find selective topics across
   the information set.

