HS2xx Family of StorageWorks FDDI Servers

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Delivers 4,300 I/O requests per second

o  HS241 provides 619 GB of online data; more than 10 Terabytes of nearline
   storage

o  Optional support for Network File Server (NFS) provides unlimited
   distributed data access

o  Centralized storage management capability minimizes FDDI traffic

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The new generation of StorageWorks FDDI managed storage servers, the HS211,
HS221, HS241, and HS280, integrate Alpha technology and modular design. This
combination lets users

o  Increase the storage capacity of an existing OpenVMS systems while using
   only one or two cluster nodes

o  Add disaster-tolerant storage to an existing FDDI cluster

o  Share critical information campus-wide while centralizing management to
   lower costs

o  Increase data security by isolating storage in a separate, secure
   location

The entry-level HS211 FDDI server consists of an Alpha server processor,
StorageWorks modular components, and high-performance, high-connectivity
device channel processors. The HS221 high-availability and HS241
high-performance models provide comprehensive redundancy and failover
through dual Alpha server processors, multiple device channel processors,
and redundant power and cooling. To maximize total capacity and flexibility,
a full range of StorageWorks devices, including magnetic and solid-state
disks, tapes, optical disks, tape loaders, and libraries, are supported.

Up to 619 GB of cluster-accessible online data can be stored and managed on
an HS241 server. With Digital TCP/IP Services for OpenVMS software, data can
be network file-served to Digital UNIX, SunOS, HP-UX, IBM AIX, SCO UNIX, and
NFS-served Pcs.

To increase effectiveness, server-based data can be managed by a wide range
of OpenVMS storage management products, including

o  Storage Library System for unattended backup and restore services

o  POLYCENTER Hierarchical Storage Manager for OpenVMS software which lowers
   costs by migrating dormant data to nearline storage

o  POLYCENTER File Optimizer to reduce disk fragmentation

o  StorageWorks RAID software for OpenVMS, for management of RAID arrays
   across FDDI device processors

BENEFITS

o  High capacity -- With up to 619 GB of online capacity and more than 10 TB
   of nearline capability, the HS2xx series meets virtually any capacity
   requirement. StorageWorks modularity ensures that the capacity of the
   HS241 servers expands as device capacities increase

o  Scalable Performance -- Up to 4,300 I/O requests per second, with a data
   transfer rate of 11.0 MB per second

o  Minimal FDDI overhead --Based on an Alpha server processor, management
   functions run on the server rather than over the FDDI to a separate
   server node. Results in fast, centralized storage management without
   excessive, performance-draining FDDI traffic.

o  Lower costs with centralized storage management --Since the FDDI server
   is an Alpha server, users can take advantage of Digital's wide range of
   OpenVMS storage management products to lower storage management costs and
   increase user and system manager productivity.

o  Distributed data access -- With its optional network file server
   capability and centralized storage management , the HS2xx series allows
   efficient access to information at lower total cost and with less network
   overhead than competing solutions.

o  Disaster protection -- Disaster protection is increased by replicating
   data at some distance from the primary data center. By using OpenVMS
   Volume Shadowing software, data can be shadowed up to 40 kilometers in a
   single FDDI network. Greater distances are possible in conjunction with
   ATM.

o  Scalable availability -- Controller-based disk mirroring, adaptive RAID
   3/5, and OpenVMS Volume Shadowing software can be combined with optional
   redundancy features to ensure the right level of availability for any
   application.

o  Investment protection -- The HS2xx StorageWorks FDDI Server line is
   positioned to evolve with growing network storage needs and to take
   advantage of technology advancements.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

All HS2xx series storage management products will be available in October
through Digital and its business partners.

For the HS211-AA/AB, HS221-AA/AB, HS241-AA/AB server models and the HS210
upgrade:

o  Each AlphaServer has 64 MB of memory

o  Each channel processor comes with a 32 MB non-volatile read/write cache,
   a write-back cache module, and the appropriate firmware license

o  Each server ships with the appropriate OpenVMS operating System, OpenVMS,
   and volume shadowing licenses, as well as software customization
   procedures for installation ease.

