Celebris XL and Alpha XL -- Digital Personal Workstation for Windows NT

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Leadership personal workstations at PC prices

o  Engineered to meet future demands for flexibility, allowing upgrades to
   faster Intel and Alpha CPUs and options

o  Choice of either RISC or CISC processors depending upon the application
   and price/performance that is right for the user

o  PC ease-of-use experience with factory-installed Windows NT software

o  Performance characterization of key applications across the entire line

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The Digital personal workstation product family, comprised of Celebris XL
Pentium models and Alpha XL models, is targeted at the rapidly expanding
market of Windows NT based workstations. The XL family uses an enhanced
minitower design, the forerunner of which was widely shipped on the Celebris
XL PC family. The XL systems come with factory-installed Windows NT software
and provide full access to those PC options supported under Microsoft's
Hardware Compatibility List (HCL) for the appropriate processor type. Using
a processor-independent, CPU daughtercard approach, all family members have
interchangeable components and are easily upgradeable, thus ensuring the
highest level of investment protection.

Benefits

o  Industry standards -- Supports both industry standard CISC CPUs and
   performance-leading 64 bit RISC CPUs, making this a superb Windows NT
   workstation platform.

o  Performance -- Supports today's leading applications in both technical
   (MCAD, ECAD, and CASE) and commercial (desktop publishing, office
   productivity, finance, and database) environments.

o  Price -- Leadership dollars per SPECmark for Windows NT systems.

o  Investment protection -- Provides future upgradability to more powerful
   CPU chips and offers the industry's best warranty.

o  Open system -- Industry-standard PCI/ISA options available through a
   variety of suppliers.

