POLYCENTER AssetWORKS V2.0

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Point-and-click software usage monitoring for PCs; saves historical
   information for analysis

o  Improved reporting capability with on-screen graphing and the ability to
   export data

o  System management from a single console; adds support for HP-UX, IBM AIX
   and Sun Solaris systems

o  Microsoft Systems Management Server V1.1 adds Windows 95 capability to PC
   platforms

o  Supports integration with POLYCENTER Manager on NetView for Windows NT

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

Often, the hidden, indirect costs of managing client/server computing
rapidly erode the cost advantages of distributed computing. POLYCENTER
AssetWORKS V2.0 provides practical solutions for automating configuration
and asset management tasks for a broad range of platforms across the
enterprise. It collects hardware and software configuration data, automates
the electronic distribution and installation of applications and software
upgrades, and monitors software usage throughout the environment.

AssetWORKS V2.0 comes prepared to measure PC desktop applications and
application suites, provides extensions to the SMS Administrator console for
defining additional applications. Metering supports both client- and
server-based applications by gathering and saving usage data and making it
available through SMS. Detached client support allows metering of software
usage on laptops, even when they are "on the road."

Features

o  The metering capability in Version 2.0 of AssetWORKS is available in the
   new POLYCENTER AssetWORKS PC Client. This client supports DOS, Windows
   3.1, Windows for Workgroups, Windows NT Alpha and Intel systems, and
   Macintosh 6800 and PowerPC systems. Support for Windows 95 and OS/2
   systems will follow in a subsequent release.

o  Metering reports are available for general software application packages,
   server applications, and site/domain applications.

o  An improved hardware/software inventory reporting capability includes
   graphical display of inventory information, ability to print hardcopies,
   and export to portable graphical formats.

o  The new interactive reporting capability features over 50 preconfigured,
   adjustable report templates. These templates may be used "as is" to
   generate reports on PC, UNIX, and OpenVMS, or customized by the SMS
   Administrator to suit individualized needs.

o  Extends SMS inventory for PCs by automatically including detailed
   inventory from DMI-enabled such as manufacturer name and firmware
   revisions.

o  The integration of AssetWORKS V 2.0 with POLYCENTER Manager on NetView
   for Windows NT provides system and network management that is easy to use
   and cost effective. AssetWORKS offers a launch with context to the new
   POLYCENTER NetView V3.0 for Windows NT product. From the SMS
   Administrator console, select a system to be managed and launch NetView
   to perform context-based network management.

o  Extends SMS client support to UNIX and OpenVMS systems. With the new UNIX
   clients in V2.0, AssetWORKS now supports Digital UNIX, Solaris, HP-UX,
   AIX, SunOS, and Ultrix.

o  Seamlessly integrates with and extends SMS and, with this release,
   Package Definition Files (PDFs) are offered for automated "drag-and-drop"
   distribution and installation of AssetWORKS PC Client components onto
   remote systems using SMS. .

BENEFITS

o  Software metering provides significant savings through better utilization
   of software assets, redeployment of licenses, and retirements for
   underutilized software

o  Usage data delivers accurate information for better planning

o  AssetWORKS metering reports may be used to verify compliance with
   software license terms and conditions

o  Software usage data enhances system security

o  End users have access to the software they need, when they need it

o  AssetWORKS gives CIOs and CFOs the information to negotiate volume
   purchases with software vendors

o  Automated configuration tools help manage costs associated with
   multivendor assets in a distributed computing environment

Availability and ordering

The U.S. product will be available on October 13, 1995; the European version
will be available on October 27, 1995.

With the Version 2.0 release of AssetWORKS, the previous POLYCENTER
AssetWORKS Agent for UNIX and OpenVMS platforms is renamed POLYCENTER
AssetWORKS Enterprise Client.  The new POLYCENTER AssetWORKS PC Client
supports software metering of the PC platforms in Version 2.0. Microsoft
Systems Management Server (SMS) Version 1.1 is a prerequisite for AssetWORKS
V 2.0. With the Version 2.0 release of AssetWORKS, the previous SMS User
License is renamed SMS Client Access License to be compatible with changes
in Microsoft terminology for SMS licensing.

