Workgroup Web Forum

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Team collaboration across the Web, corporate Internet, or TCP/IP LAN

o  Organize information to fit business need

o  Participate in online conferencing; use polling capabilities

o  Server-based Internet style application for Windows NT and Digital UNIX

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

Workgroup Web Forum combines team collaboration with Internet technology to
provide file sharing and online conferencing anywhere in a corporate network
or the Internet by letting teams of users easily upload, organize, and
distribute information in a variety of formats. Users create descriptive
folders and document names that are easily recognizable and accessible by
all team members.  Those folders and documents are connected through
hyperlinks that span from local server-based repositories to the World Wide
Web. Workgroup Web Forum automatically manages the hyperlinks, allowing the
quick and easy association of distributed information.

Any HTML-compliant web browser (NCSA Mosaic and browsers from Spyglass,
Netscape, Spry, IBM, Apple, and other vendors) running on PC's, Macintoshes,
or UNIX platforms, can be used to gain access to and interact within the
forums.

Workgroup Web Forum coexists with popular HTTP servers such as NCSA HTTPd,
Purveyor, and Netscape Communications Server, and enhances them by providing
interactive collaborative applications usable right out-of-the-box, the
ability to customize the implementation and to change or improve the
collaborative environment. Administrative tools provide for secure
management of content and access control lists, ensuring that only
authorized users have read and/or write access to files and documents.

A Software Developer's Kit (SDK) is included, which permits users to modify
the applications provided or develop entirely new collaborative
applications. Based on the Tcl scripting language, users can customize and
implement Web applications on an accelerated development cycle when compared
to traditional applications development cycles.

BENEFITS

o  Online conferencing -- Allows users to conduct and participate in
   multiple electronic conferences.

o  Realtime polling -- Gives discussion groups a mechanism to reach
   consensus on key issues. Polling results can be displayed graphically, at
   a glance.

o  Organized information -- Lets users organize information into folders,
   documents, and discussions. Since these are familiar concepts, users
   immediately understand how to use them.

o  Security -- Provides the access controls needed to conduct business over
   the Internet. The administrator authorizes read and/or write privileges
   to documents, folders, and conferences.

o  Find information easily -- Provides keyword and content-based retrieval
   capabilties to help users find information quickly. A "what's new"
   feature checks for recently generated material.

o  Support for heterogeneous environments -- Accessible by any PC,
   Macintosh, or UNIX workstation with a Mosaic browser; no specialized
   client software is needed.

o  Existing technology -- Means fewer changes for the end user, training
   needs are kept at a minimum.

o  Easy installation and startup -- Includes collaborative applications that
   are usable right away.

o  Easy application modification and expansion --Workgroup Web Forum
   Software Developer's Kit lets developers offer customized,
   business-specific solutions to their users.

PRODUCT POSITIONING

Workgroup Web and Workgroup Web Forum are a family of products that provide
team communication and collaboration.

Workgroup Web is a Windows based PC application that lets team members
access information on the desktop and across shared directories in a LAN/WAN
environment. An Internet connection is not required. Users can easily
install and use Workgroup Web, and an administrator is not required. (See
the"Workgroup Web V1.0 for Windows" in this issue of Customer Update.)

Workgroup Web Forum is a server-based collaborative applications suite that
runs on corporate IP and Internet-based HTTP servers. Some of its additional
features are enhanced search capabilities, automatic access auditing,
embedded security, and a tool kit for customization.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

Available on October 2, 1995, Workgroup Web Forum is a PC-style,
shrink-wrapped package that includes the license, software media (CD-ROM),
and documentation. One license is required for each server. There are no
license limits to the numbers of clients who can access the server.

For the remainder of 1995, each Workgroup Web Forum will include, at no
extra cost, a fully licensed version of Workgroup Web V1.0 for Windows, and
a CD-ROM that contains public domain Internet software.

